From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:50:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: gadget: Leave clock gating on a USB reset

A host may reset a device whose bus it suspended, without resuming it
first. In device mode with clock gating (power_down NONE, as on Apple
SoCs), the suspend interrupt gates the PHY clock and hclk, and sets
lx_state to L2. The USB reset interrupt that follows leaves both in
place. dwc2_hsotg_core_init_disconnected() then queues the EP0 setup
request, which dwc2_hsotg_ep_queue() refuses outside L0:

  dwc2 ...: dwc2_hsotg_enqueue_setup: failed queue (-11)

This repeats on every further reset, and the device never enumerates
until the UDC is unbound and bound again. An Apple iPad 5 (A9) showed
it on every boot of one kernel, 36 times per boot; a Mac host saw no
device.

Leave clock gating and enter L0 on the USB reset before EP0 is armed
again, as the RESETDET branch does for partial power down, and as
Apple's own device controller driver does on reset (it ungates the
clocks, then arms EP0).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
index fbc5075..0c6e60f 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -3768,6 +3768,24 @@ irq_retry:
 
 		dwc2_writel(hsotg, GINTSTS_USBRST, GINTSTS);
 
+		/*
+		 * A reset of a suspended bus.  No resume came first, so a core
+		 * that entered clock gating on the suspend is still gated and
+		 * in L2, and dwc2_hsotg_ep_queue() refuses the EP0 setup
+		 * request that dwc2_hsotg_core_init_disconnected() queues
+		 * (-EAGAIN) on this and every later reset, until the UDC is
+		 * rebound.  Leave clock gating and return to L0 first, as the
+		 * RESETDET branch above does for partial power down.
+		 */
+		if (hsotg->lx_state == DWC2_L2 && !hsotg->in_ppd) {
+			if (hsotg->params.power_down ==
+			    DWC2_POWER_DOWN_PARAM_NONE && hsotg->bus_suspended &&
+			    !hsotg->params.no_clock_gating)
+				dwc2_gadget_exit_clock_gating(hsotg, 0);
+			else
+				hsotg->lx_state = DWC2_L0;
+		}
+
 		/* Report disconnection if it is not already done. */
 		dwc2_hsotg_disconnect(hsotg);
 
